Scriptname NEC Native Hidden
{The Papyrus API of Native Equipment Condition, for mods that read or change the condition of weapons, armor and food. Every function is global: call NEC.GetCondition(akItem).}

; # What this is
; NEC is the script Native Equipment Condition ships. Other mods call its functions to read and change the
; condition of weapons and armor, the freshness of food, the repair costs and the curves, and hear its events.
;
; Compile against NEC.psc, which NEC installs in Data\Scripts\Source\User: keep that folder among your import
; folders. Never ship a copy of NEC.pex or NEC.psc with your mod.
;
; GetVersion tells you which NEC.dll runs, GetScriptVersion which NEC.pex your game loaded.
;
; NEC.papyrus.log, in Documents\My Games\Fallout4\F4SE\NEC, logs the errors in a script's calls to NEC.
;
; # How an item is named
; Every item function takes an ObjectReference akItem, and 3 things fit in it:
; 1. An item lying in the world, as any reference to it.
; 2. A persistent item inside a container or an inventory, such as a quest item or Self in a script on the item.
; 3. A handle NEC gives you for 1 stack inside a container or an inventory, from GetItems, GetEquippedWeapon,
;    GetWornItem or GetWornItems. Papyrus prints one as [ObjectReference <Item 2 in container  (00000014)>].
;
; A handle names 1 stack while a script variable holds it. It follows its stack into another container and back,
; out into the world as that world item, and across a save and a load.
;
; Once no script holds it any more, the game takes the stack's number off within seconds, so ask GetItems again.
;
; Once the stack no longer exists, because it was consumed, scrapped or removed, a handle answers None, false or -1.
; The game may later give that number to an item that arrives in the same container, so drop a handle you no longer
; need.
;
; Identical new copies share 1 stack, so GetCount can be above 1. A write, a wear or a repair changes 1 copy of such
; a stack: that copy splits off and your handle follows it. Call GetItems again for the rest.
;
; A pile lying in the world shares 1 condition between its copies, and a write changes all of them.
;
; # Units
; Condition and freshness are a percent from 0 to 100, with decimals: the API gives 85.3 where the item card shows 85.
; A new item reads 100. -1 means NEC gives this item no condition, or akItem is None or no longer exists.
; The curve functions below, GetDamageShare to GetJamChance, answer a fraction from 0 to 1: the share of its damage a
; weapon keeps, or the chance a magazine jams. Vanilla's GetItemHealthPercent is a fraction from 0 to 1 too, not a
; percent.
;
; # Writes
; A write works on gear NEC gives a condition, see IsTracked, and returns false for anything else. A write costs the
; player nothing: no perk, workbench, component or caps are needed. If your mod should charge for a repair, work the
; price out with the repair economics functions below.
;
; A write goes through even when the player turned wear off in MCM. Wear scales by NEC's wear rate sliders, the
; other writes apply the value as given. An item on a list in NEC/Exclude is never written.
;
; After a write, the item card, the Pip-Boy row and a worn piece's protection follow, and the player's weapon
; brought to 0 is put away as wear puts it away. An open bench or barter screen shows the change once it lists the
; item again.
;
; # When a call runs
; Every function but GetVersion, GetVersionString and GetScriptVersion is latent: it runs on the next Papyrus tick,
; during play and while a menu pauses the game, and returns when its work is done. So a call takes about 1 frame,
; and a script that calls in a loop advances 1 call per frame. The 3 version functions return at once.
;
; A call fails safely when the game locks that item's inventory for more than 5 ms, and during a save, a load or a
; quit to the main menu: it answers as if the item no longer existed and writes nothing. NEC.papyrus.log records
; each such call. A save made while a script was inside a call to NEC loads only with NEC installed, since without
; NEC the game refuses it as corrupt.
;
; # Versions
; 10900 is 1.9.0, the first NEC with this script.

; # Functions

; ## Version

; The version of NEC.dll as 1 number, major times 10000 plus minor times 100 plus patch: 10900 for 1.9.0.
int Function GetVersion() global native

; The version of NEC.dll as text: "1.9.0".
string Function GetVersionString() global native

; The version this NEC.pex belongs to, equal to GetVersion when the DLL and NEC.pex come from 1 release.
int Function GetScriptVersion() global
    return ${NEC_VERSION_NUMBER}
EndFunction

; ## Features and settings

; True when the NEC feature of this name runs: its NEC.ini switch is on and no other DLL took all of it. Names: see Feature names.
bool Function IsFeatureOn(string asFeature) global native

; True when another DLL took some or all of this feature, as NEC's main MCM page and NEC.log say.
bool Function IsFeatureTakenOver(string asFeature) global native

; A decimal setting by its MCM id, key:section, such as "fWearRateMult:Balance". 0.0 for an id NEC does not know.
float Function GetSettingFloat(string asId) global native

; A whole number setting by its MCM id, such as "iFreeMendAbove:Balance". 0 for an id NEC does not know.
int Function GetSettingInt(string asId) global native

; A switch by its MCM id, such as "bFoodSpoils:Features". False for an id NEC does not know.
bool Function GetSettingBool(string asId) global native

; ## Naming items

; 1 handle per stack of akBase akHolder carries, akBase None for every weapon, armor and food NEC tracks. None for a
; None holder or one whose inventory the game has not loaded.
ObjectReference[] Function GetItems(ObjectReference akHolder, Form akBase) global native

; A handle to the weapon in akActor's hands, None when they hold none NEC tracks.
ObjectReference Function GetEquippedWeapon(Actor akActor) global native

; A handle to the tracked piece akActor wears on biped slot aiSlot, 30 to 61, None when there is none.
ObjectReference Function GetWornItem(Actor akActor, int aiSlot) global native

; 1 handle per tracked piece akActor wears, an empty array for none or an actor in power armor.
ObjectReference[] Function GetWornItems(Actor akActor) global native

; The container or actor holding akItem, None for an item lying in the world.
ObjectReference Function GetHolder(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; The base form of akItem, its Weapon, Armor or Potion record.
Form Function GetBase(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; How many copies akItem's stack holds, 0 for None or an item that no longer exists.
int Function GetCount(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; ## Reading condition

; True when NEC gives this weapon or armor a condition.
bool Function IsTracked(Form akBase) global native

; Why NEC gives akBase no condition, as NEC.log words it, such as "on a list in NEC/Exclude". "" when it does.
string Function WhyNotTracked(Form akBase) global native

; akItem's condition, a percent from 0 to 100, -1 when NEC gives it none.
float Function GetCondition(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; True when akItem is at 0 condition, so the game will not equip it.
bool Function IsBroken(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; True for loot lying in the world that rolls its condition when someone first takes or looks at it. It reads 100.
bool Function IsUnrolled(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; ## Changing condition

; Sets akItem's condition to afPercent, kept between 0 and 100. True once the item is at that condition.
bool Function SetCondition(ObjectReference akItem, float afPercent) global native

; Takes afPercent points off akItem's condition, down to 0 at most. True once written.
bool Function Damage(ObjectReference akItem, float afPercent) global native

; Adds afPercent points to akItem's condition, up to 100 at most. True once written.
bool Function Repair(ObjectReference akItem, float afPercent) global native

; Wears akItem as afUses shots or swings would, armor as that many hits as hard as an ordinary weapon's, at NEC's rate.
; The rate is this item's for its holder, wear rate sliders included.
bool Function Wear(ObjectReference akItem, float afUses = 1.0) global native

; Rolls unrolled loot lying in the world as the player's pickup would. False when it already rolled, while Worn loot
; is off, or for a trader's or a faction's item, which rolls when it is taken.
bool Function RollCondition(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; ## Curves

; The share of its damage a weapon keeps at afPercent, from 0 to 1, from fDamageFloor at 0 to 1 at fWeaponPenaltyStart times 100.
float Function GetDamageShare(float afPercent) global native

; The share of its protection a piece of armor keeps at afPercent, from fArmorFloor at 0 to 1 at fArmorPenaltyStart times 100.
float Function GetArmorShare(float afPercent) global native

; The share of its accuracy the gun akWeapon keeps at afPercent, 1 for anything that is not a gun.
float Function GetAccuracyShare(Form akWeapon, float afPercent) global native

; The share of its range the gun akWeapon keeps at afPercent, 1 for anything that is not a gun.
float Function GetRangeShare(Form akWeapon, float afPercent) global native

; The share of its fire rate the automatic weapon akWeapon keeps at afPercent, with its mods, 1 for any other.
float Function GetFireRateShare(ObjectReference akWeapon, float afPercent) global native

; The share of its critical meter charge a weapon keeps at afPercent, from fCritMeterFloor at 0 to 1 at fWeaponPenaltyStart times 100.
float Function GetCritShare(float afPercent) global native

; The share of its price an item keeps at afPercent, along fValueExponent.
float Function GetPriceShare(float afPercent) global native

; The chance a magazine of a gun at afPercent jams, from 0 to 1, 0 at fJamStart times 100 and above.
float Function GetJamChance(float afPercent) global native

; The condition points 1 Wear takes off akItem at its holder's wear speed, -1 for an untracked item.
float Function GetWearPerUse(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; ## Repair economics

; The Free mend above setting: a repair of an item above this percent costs nothing at the bench.
int Function GetFreeMendAbove() global native

; The Mod lock below setting: the bench modifies no item below this percent.
int Function GetModLockBelow() global native

; How many percent the player's crafting perk rank takes off a bench repair of akBase, 0 to 50.
int Function GetRepairDiscount(Form akBase) global native

; 1 component of a bill and how many of it.
Struct Cost
    Component object
    int count
EndStruct

; The components the bench would take from the player to bring akItem to aiToPercent, empty for a free mend, None when the bench would not repair it.
Cost[] Function GetRepairCost(ObjectReference akItem, int aiToPercent) global native

; The components akItem scraps into at the bench at its condition, with the player's perks.
Cost[] Function GetScrapYield(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; The condition points the player's spare akSpare restores to the player's akItem, -1 when it is no spare for it.
int Function GetSpareGain(ObjectReference akItem, ObjectReference akSpare) global native

; How far akTrader repairs akBase's kind of gear, a percent, 0 when they repair none of it.
int Function GetTraderRepairLevel(Actor akTrader, Form akBase) global native

; The caps akTrader asks to repair akItem to aiToPercent, -1 when they would not.
int Function GetTraderRepairPrice(Actor akTrader, ObjectReference akItem, int aiToPercent) global native

; ## Food

; akFood's kind: -1 not food, 0 never spoils, 1 raw, 2 crop, 3 cooked.
int Function GetFoodKind(Form akFood) global native

; How many game days akFood stays fresh outside a fridge at the current settings, -1 for food that never spoils.
float Function GetSpoilDays(Form akFood) global native

; akItem's freshness, a percent, 0 once spoiled, -1 for food that never spoils or while food spoiling is off.
float Function GetFreshness(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; The game days until akItem spoils outside a fridge, 0 once spoiled, -1 where GetFreshness answers -1.
float Function GetDaysLeft(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; Sets the freshness of akItem's whole stack to afPercent, above 0 and up to 100. True once written.
bool Function SetFreshness(ObjectReference akItem, float afPercent) global native

; Turns akItem's whole stack spoiled, as running out of time does. True once written.
bool Function Spoil(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; True when akItem has spoiled or its time ran out.
bool Function IsSpoiled(ObjectReference akItem) global native

; True when food in akContainer keeps as in a fridge.
bool Function IsFridge(ObjectReference akContainer) global native

; ## Helpers
; Plain Papyrus on the functions above, for the jobs most mods write themselves. Import NEC, or call them as
; NEC.GetItemsBelow(...). Each takes 1 frame per item it touches, as the functions it calls do.

; Shows "<name>: <condition>%" on screen, or "<name>: no condition" for an item NEC leaves alone.
Function SayCondition(ObjectReference akItem) global
    Form base = GetBase(akItem)
    string name = "None"
    If base != None
        name = base.GetName()
    EndIf
    float condition = GetCondition(akItem)
    If condition < 0.0
        Debug.Notification(name + ": no condition")
    Else
        Debug.Notification(name + ": " + (condition as int) + "%")
    EndIf
EndFunction

; Writes every item NEC tracks in akHolder to the Papyrus log, 1 line each: name, count, condition.
Function TraceItems(ObjectReference akHolder) global
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akHolder, None)
    If items == None
        Debug.Trace("NEC: " + akHolder + " has no loaded inventory")
        Return
    EndIf
    int i = 0
    While i < items.Length
        Form base = GetBase(items[i])
        If base != None
            Debug.Trace("NEC: " + base.GetName() + " x" + GetCount(items[i]) + " at " + GetCondition(items[i]) + "%")
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
EndFunction

; The items of akHolder below afPercent, worst first. Empty when there are none or the inventory is not loaded.
ObjectReference[] Function GetItemsBelow(ObjectReference akHolder, float afPercent) global
    ObjectReference[] out = new ObjectReference[0]
    float[] conditions = new float[0]
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akHolder, None)
    If items == None
        Return out
    EndIf
    int i = 0
    While i < items.Length
        float condition = GetCondition(items[i])
        If condition >= 0.0 && condition < afPercent
            int at = 0
            While at < conditions.Length && conditions[at] <= condition
                at += 1
            EndWhile
            out.Insert(items[i], at)
            conditions.Insert(condition, at)
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return out
EndFunction

; The items of akHolder at 0.
ObjectReference[] Function GetBrokenItems(ObjectReference akHolder) global
    ObjectReference[] out = new ObjectReference[0]
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akHolder, None)
    If items == None
        Return out
    EndIf
    int i = 0
    While i < items.Length
        If IsBroken(items[i])
            out.Add(items[i])
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return out
EndFunction

; The worn piece of akActor with the lowest condition, None when nothing worn has one.
ObjectReference Function GetWeakestWornItem(Actor akActor) global
    ObjectReference[] worn = GetWornItems(akActor)
    ObjectReference weakest = None
    float lowest = 101.0
    int i = 0
    While worn != None && i < worn.Length
        float condition = GetCondition(worn[i])
        If condition >= 0.0 && condition < lowest
            lowest = condition
            weakest = worn[i]
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return weakest
EndFunction

; The condition of the weapon in akActor's hands, -1 for none.
float Function GetEquippedWeaponCondition(Actor akActor) global
    Return GetCondition(GetEquippedWeapon(akActor))
EndFunction

; The average condition of what akActor wears, -1 when nothing worn has one.
float Function GetWornCondition(Actor akActor) global
    ObjectReference[] worn = GetWornItems(akActor)
    float sum = 0.0
    int counted = 0
    int i = 0
    While worn != None && i < worn.Length
        float condition = GetCondition(worn[i])
        If condition >= 0.0
            sum += condition
            counted += 1
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    If counted == 0
        Return -1.0
    EndIf
    Return sum / counted
EndFunction

; Repairs every item of akHolder below afTo up to it. How many it repaired.
int Function RepairAll(ObjectReference akHolder, float afTo = 100.0) global
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItemsBelow(akHolder, afTo)
    int done = 0
    int i = 0
    While i < items.Length
        If SetCondition(items[i], afTo)
            done += 1
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return done
EndFunction

; Takes afPercent off every item NEC tracks in akHolder. How many it damaged.
int Function DamageAll(ObjectReference akHolder, float afPercent) global
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akHolder, None)
    int done = 0
    int i = 0
    While items != None && i < items.Length
        If Damage(items[i], afPercent)
            done += 1
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return done
EndFunction

; Wears every piece akActor wears by afUses uses, along NEC's armor curve. How many pieces it wore.
int Function WearWorn(Actor akActor, float afUses = 1.0) global
    ObjectReference[] worn = GetWornItems(akActor)
    int done = 0
    int i = 0
    While worn != None && i < worn.Length
        If Wear(worn[i], afUses)
            done += 1
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return done
EndFunction

; Spoils every food in akContainer that is not spoiled yet. How many it spoiled.
int Function SpoilAll(ObjectReference akContainer) global
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akContainer, None)
    int done = 0
    int i = 0
    While items != None && i < items.Length
        If GetFreshness(items[i]) >= 0.0 && !IsSpoiled(items[i]) && Spoil(items[i])
            done += 1
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return done
EndFunction

; The spoiled food in akContainer.
ObjectReference[] Function GetSpoiledFood(ObjectReference akContainer) global
    ObjectReference[] out = new ObjectReference[0]
    ObjectReference[] items = GetItems(akContainer, None)
    int i = 0
    While items != None && i < items.Length
        If IsSpoiled(items[i])
            out.Add(items[i])
        EndIf
        i += 1
    EndWhile
    Return out
EndFunction

; # Feature names
; IsFeatureOn and IsFeatureTakenOver take the name of a feature that another DLL can take over, and
; NEC_Papyrus_API.txt lists them. Armor wear has none: ask GetSettingFloat("fArmorWearRateMult:Balance"), 0 when the
; player's armor never wears.

; # Events
; NEC sends its events through F4SE. Register once, in OnInit for example, and F4SE keeps the registration in its
; own save: RegisterForExternalEvent("NEC:Broke", "OnNECBroke"). F4SE calls your Function by name, so declare it
; with exactly these parameter types. akItem is a handle as GetItems gives, None when that stack no longer exists by then.
;
; Most events reach you within about 1 frame. One from a loot roll or a food arrival waits for NEC's next shot, hit,
; menu or call to any NEC function but GetScriptVersion. One whose holder's inventory the game holds is tried again
; at each of them. After at least 2 s and 100 tries it comes with akItem None. Events of 1 holder come in the order
; they happened. None comes during a save load, and a load that fails can lose the events waiting then.
;
; If more than 256 events wait, NEC drops the newest and NEC.papyrus.log counts them.
;
; Event NEC:ConditionChanged
; Function OnConditionChanged(ObjectReference akHolder, Form akBase, ObjectReference akItem, float afBefore, float afAfter, int aiCause)
; The condition of an item the player carries changed. aiCause: 0 wear, 1 repair, 2 a script, 3 the loot roll of an item that
; reaches you still unrolled (afBefore 100), 4 the console.
;
; Event NEC:Broke
; Function OnBroke(ObjectReference akHolder, Form akBase, ObjectReference akItem)
; A weapon or a piece of armor reached 0 condition, anybody's. akHolder is None for an item lying in the world.
;
; Event NEC:Jammed
; Function OnJammed(Actor akActor, Form akWeapon, ObjectReference akItem)
; The player's gun jammed.
;
; Event NEC:FoodSpoiled
; Function OnFoodSpoiled(ObjectReference akHolder, Form akFood, int aiCount)
; aiCount pieces of akFood were turned spoiled, in anybody's inventory or container. NEC does this as a menu shows the
; food or the food changes hands, so IsSpoiled can answer true before the event comes.

; # Examples
; Read the condition of the weapon in the player's hands:
;
;   Function SayWeaponCondition() global
;       ObjectReference item = NEC.GetEquippedWeapon(Game.GetPlayer())
;       If item != None
;           Debug.Notification("Weapon condition " + NEC.GetCondition(item))
;       EndIf
;   EndFunction
;
; Repair every weapon and piece of armor a container holds:
;
;   Function RepairEveryCopy(ObjectReference akContainer) global
;       ObjectReference[] items = NEC.GetItems(akContainer, None)
;       If items == None
;           Return
;       EndIf
;       int index = 0
;       While index < items.Length
;           float condition = NEC.GetCondition(items[index])
;           If condition >= 0.0 && condition < 100.0
;               NEC.SetCondition(items[index], 100.0)
;           EndIf
;           index += 1
;       EndWhile
;   EndFunction
;
; React to NEC:Broke, in a quest script:
;
;   Scriptname MyBrokeWatcher extends Quest
;
;   Event OnInit()
;       RegisterForExternalEvent("NEC:Broke", "OnNECBroke")
;   EndEvent
;
;   Function OnNECBroke(ObjectReference akHolder, Form akBase, ObjectReference akItem)
;       If akHolder == Game.GetPlayer()
;           Debug.Notification("Something you carry broke")
;       EndIf
;   EndFunction
